---
import AppShell from '../../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { ORGANIZATION_REF, SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL, WEBSITE_REF } from '../../lib/seo';

export const prerender = true;

const title = 'AI Automation Services for Small Teams | Neil Busque';
const description = 'Neil Busque maps the repetitive work slowing your team down, then builds the AI agents and workflows that handle it. Based in New Jersey.';
const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/ai-automation-services';

const service = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': `${canonical}#service`,
  name: 'AI Automation Services',
  url: canonical,
  image: SOCIAL_IMAGE_URL,
  provider: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  brand: ORGANIZATION_REF,
  isPartOf: WEBSITE_REF,
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': `${canonical}#webpage` },
  areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  serviceType: ['AI automation', 'Workflow automation', 'Business process automation', 'CRM automation', 'AI agent development'],
  description,
};
---
<AppShell title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} active="services">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
      { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
      { name: 'AI Automation Services', url: canonical },
    ]} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(service)} />
  </Fragment>

  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="idx">&#8727;</span> Services &#183; AI Automation</p>
    <h1>AI automation <span class="accent">services</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I build automations for small teams in New Jersey, New York, and across the US. The job is simple: find the repeated work that keeps stealing time, then build a dependable way to handle it.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="article-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I usually automate</h2>
      <p>Most teams do not need another big platform. They need a few specific jobs to stop depending on memory and copy-paste. These come up most often:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Leads.</strong> Capture, enrich, route, and follow up automatically, so nothing sits in an inbox going cold.</li>
        <li><strong>Follow-up and nurture.</strong> Email and SMS sequences triggered by what people actually do, not by a calendar.</li>
        <li><strong>Ops and admin.</strong> Data entry, enrichment, reporting, CRM hygiene, and the handoffs between tools that quietly eat hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Research and content.</strong> Agents that read, summarize, and draft on a schedule so a person only has to edit.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Plain automation or an AI agent</h2>
      <p>Not everything needs AI. If the steps never change, a normal workflow is cheaper and easier to trust. I add an agent when the task involves messy input, a real decision, or a draft a person should review. <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">Here is how I build those agents.</a></p>

      <h2>How the work runs</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>We find the time sink.</strong> On one call, we trace where the work slows down and what people keep doing by hand.</li>
        <li><strong>I scope it before I build.</strong> You see exactly what gets automated and what does not, so nothing about the finished build surprises you.</li>
        <li><strong>I build it.</strong> Days, not quarters, and you see progress as it goes.</li>
        <li><strong>You keep it or I keep running it.</strong> Your choice. It is your system either way.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Why one person instead of an agency</h2>
      <p>Automations need maintenance. A webhook changes, an API removes a field, or your process changes. When that happens, you message the person who built it. There is no account-manager relay.</p>

      <h2>Where I work</h2>
      <p>I am based in Elizabeth, New Jersey and work with teams across the NJ and NYC metro, plus remote clients across the United States. Most of the work is remote regardless of where you are, and I am reachable in Eastern time.</p>

      <h2>See the work first</h2>
      <p>In 2026 I shipped more than 40 web apps, AI agents, and automations. Before that, I shipped over 20 production n8n workflows across more than 10 client accounts, including an onboarding system that cut a 30-day process to 7 days. Browse <a href="/work">the work</a> and <a href="/resources">the guides</a> before you decide anything.</p>

      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <p>Tell me where your team loses hours and I will tell you honestly whether automation is the right fix. <a href="/contact">Send me the problem</a>, or see <a href="/services/ai-automation-consultant">what an AI automation consultant does</a> and <a href="/services/ai-agent-development">how AI agent development works</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="hire-cta v8-card">
    <span class="eyebrow">The guarantee</span>
    <p class="guarantee">I keep working until you are proud of it. If I am not the right fit, I will tell you on the first call.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn-sun" href="/contact">Tell me what you need</a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://wa.me/19083164140?text=Hi%20Neil%2C%20I%20want%20to%20talk%20about%20a%20build">Or message on WhatsApp</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>
